      "source": [
        "## Checkpoint cache\n",
        "Every completed epoch saves model weights, Adam state, metric history, and PyTorch/data-loader random states. Writes replace the previous checkpoint only after the new file is fully written. Configuration, seed, dataset ID, data sizes, transforms, and experiment name determine the cache filename.\n",
        "\n",
        "To inspect a checkpoint without training:\n",
        "```python\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "saved_run = load_experiment(next(Path(CACHE_DIR).glob(\"*.pt\")))\n",
        "print(saved_run[\"config\"], saved_run[\"complete\"])\n",
        "print(saved_run[\"history\"])\n",
        "```\n",
        "To force a fresh run, pass `resume=False`. Change `dataset_id` if data, splits, or preprocessing change; increment `CACHE_VERSION` if you edit model/training code. Dataset contents are not automatically hashed. Keep the same cache folder when restarting.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Colab:** mount Google Drive and set `CACHE_DIR = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/lenet_cache\"` before training if the cache must survive a runtime reset. Files in Colab's temporary local storage may disappear. Atomic replacement depends on the storage filesystem's guarantees. GPU/device changes can affect reproducibility.\n"
      ]
